CASE receipt-bypass
  CommitSaveRequest.save_operation_id is Option<String>.
  commit_document_save validates the durable receipt only inside `if let Some`.
  Existing dispatcher test invokes commit with None after a Core edit and without a guarded write; it passes and marks revision 1 persisted while the disk still contains the old bytes.

CASE linux-save-as-race
  cfg(not(target_os = "macos")) create_if_absent calls std::fs::rename.
  On POSIX/Linux rename replaces an existing destination; it is not no-replace.
  A target created after the line-180 existence precheck can therefore be overwritten.

CASE stale-save-after-reload
  Save receipt/commit identity has session, document and revision but no lifecycle epoch.
  reload preserves session/document, resets revision to zero and does not wait for or invalidate `saving`.
  A prepared old-generation operation can write after explicit discard/reload; if the new generation reaches the same revision, old payload commit can mark different current text persisted.

CASE unicode-resync
  direct output: diffText("😀", "😁") => [{"from":1,"to":2,"insert":"\\ude01"}]
  from=1 is inside the UTF-16 surrogate pair and Core rejects the recovery patch as invalid-boundary.

CASE paste-resync-provenance
  normal compose attaches raw paste provenance by string search.
  resync instead rebuilds a diff from two normalized strings; diffText has no explicit EOL provenance.
  discardPendingChanges clears ChangeSets but leaves pendingPasteProvenance queued.

CASE net-zero-batch
  when composed changes are empty, sendFrame clears pendingCount and returns idle but does not clear unresolvedOptimistic.
  type+delete within one batch can therefore remain dirty indefinitely despite editor text equalling Core.
